      "claim_affected": "randomised intervention contrast",
      "evidence_state": "RECORDED",
      "source_fields": [
        "/arm_contrast/trials"
      ],
      "rendered_text": "<div class='absent'><strong>Randomised-contrast disclosure (per pooled trial, from the registry arm structure &mdash; disclosed, not an adjustment).</strong> Eligibility should test what actually DIFFERS between the randomised arms, not the mere presence of the drug word: a trial giving the drug of interest as BACKGROUND in every arm (e.g. all arms on the same agent, randomising a different drug) is not a randomised comparison of it. For each pooled trial the randomised contrast is reconstructed from AACT <code>design_groups</code> + <code>interventions</code>: <strong>4 of 4</strong> pooled trials have a registry-confirmed contrast (the intervention of interest differs across arms). A trial with no registry arm data, or coded under a class label / development code we cannot machine-match, is shown as <em>contrast unverified</em> &mdash; a VISIBLE fail-open state, never silently treated as verified. <table class='arms'><tr><th>Trial</th><th>Contrast status</th><th>Randomised difference</th></tr><tr><td>19717844</td><td>randomised contrast verified</td><td title='the intervention of interest DIFFERS across the randomised arms (registry-confirmed contrast)'>dabigatran dose 1; dabigatran dose 2; warfarin</td></tr><tr><td>21830957</td><td>randomised contrast verified</td><td title='the intervention of interest DIFFERS across the randomised arms (registry-confirmed contrast)'>rivaroxaban; warfarin</td></tr><tr><td>21870978</td><td>randomised contrast verified</td><td title='the intervention of interest DIFFERS across the randomised arms (registry-confirmed contrast)'>apixaban; warfarin</td></tr><tr><td>24251359</td><td>randomised contrast verified</td><td title='the intervention of interest DIFFERS across the randomised arms (registry-confirmed contrast)'>edoxaban tablets (high dose regimen-60mg); edoxaban tablets (low dose regimen-30mg); warfarin tablets</td></tr></table></div>",
      "text_sha256": "8a38b0bd80ded950a2ee27d9f619fb921c482472efb399fa3792c05882fa245a",
